Kubernetes driver: copy the sandbox template's labels onto the supervisor pod.
With the sandbox runtime, v0.1.3 puts template labels only on the workload
pod. The supervisor pod (os-supervisor-<sandbox-id>) makes every upstream
connection and alone holds the SPIFFE Workload API socket, but carries only
fixed openshell.ai labels. So a SPIRE ClusterSPIFFEID cannot build an ID from
labels the caller chose (here agents.garvey.sh/type), and no other label
selector can tell supervisors apart.

The patch reads the labels from the Sandbox resource's pod template, so the
create and restart paths agree. Template labels under openshell.ai or a
subdomain of it are dropped, and the control labels are applied last, so
boundary-role, boundary-pair, component and sandbox-id, which the driver's
identity checks and NetworkPolicies select on, cannot be replaced. Unit tests
cover both.

